  concept: 'Authored objective: Complete keyed service assembly.

    Authored requirement:
    Lock the CPU, cross-mount the cooler, latch both memory modules and secure the
    workshop drive.

    General teaching principle: Memory and initialization workflows
    require checking power, connectivity, configuration and the authored test responses
    in the correct sequence.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish
    that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A staged startup checklist helps distinguish a missing prerequisite from
    a later failure.
